# An object: in category theory, one of the two primitive things, a node that morphisms run between. An object has no
# internal structure of its own; all that can be said about it is said through the morphisms into and out of it. Sets,
# groups, spaces, and types are each the objects of a category. The form carries an opaque identity; what an object is
# is determined entirely by its morphisms, developed in the category files.
form object
  link identity, note private
